   440	## Lemma: Rare-history essential-sup separation
   441	Status: proved
   442	Assumptions: Singleton public-exogenous infinite process; expected-regret criterion; raw infinite-process \(\beta(h)\); integer \(H\ge1\).
   443	Statement: There exists an exogenous process with
   444	\[
   445	\beta(h)=1\quad\forall h<\infty,\qquad
   446	\sup_T V_T\le4,\qquad
   447	\sup_T\Delta_T(H)\le C/H,
   448	\]
   449	and the zero-quote learner has bounded expected regret.
   450	Construction and proof sketch: Let \(N\ge1\) have \(p_n=\Pr(N=n)=3\cdot4^{-n}\). Choose distinct \(x_n\in(0,1/4)\), set \(L_n=2^n\), and define
   451	\[
   452	P_1=x_N,\quad P_2=\cdots=P_{L_N+1}=0,\quad P_{L_N+2}=1,\quad P_t=0\text{ afterward}.
   453	\]
   454	Write \(S_n=L_n+2\). Conditioning on the positive-probability atom \(P_1=x_n\) with \(2^n+1>h\), quote \(1/2\) at \(t=1\); then \(\tau_1(1/2)=2^n+1\) surely, so \(\beta(h)=1\). For \(T\),
   455	\[
   456	V_T=\sup_a\mathbb E\sum_{t\le T}r_t(a)
   457	=\sum_{n:S_n\le T}p_n(S_n-1)\le4,
   458	\]
   459	with the supremum approached by \(a\uparrow1\). Truncation loses exactly \((S_n-1-H)_+\) quotes on atom \(N=n\), hence
   460	\[
   461	\Delta_T(H)=\delta_T(H)
   462	=\sum_{n:S_n\le T}p_n(S_n-1-H)_+
   463	\le \sum_n 3\cdot4^{-n}(2^n+1-H)_+
   464	\le C/H.
   465	\]
   466	Known gaps: This is expected regret only. On the rare atom \(N=n\), pathwise regret at \(T=S_n\) is order \(2^n\). It is not a finite-horizon \(\beta_T\) statement and not a minimax lower-bound construction.
   467	Source: `iterations/iter_007/idea_02/explorer_01.md`; `iterations/iter_007/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md`.
