   609	## Lemma: Last-exceedance fixed-quote identity
   610	Status: proved
   611	Assumptions: Finite horizon \(T\); fixed price path; quote \(a\in[0,1]\); future-only trade event.
   612	Statement: Let
   613	\[
   614	L_a=\max\{s\le T:P_s>a\},
   615	\]
   616	with \(L_a=0\) if no such \(s\) exists. Then
   617	\[
   618	r_t(a)=a{\bf 1}\{L_a>t\},\qquad
   619	\sum_{t=1}^T r_t(a)=a(L_a-1)_+.
   620	\]
   621	Proof sketch: A quote posted at time \(t\) trades by horizon \(T\) iff some future price \(P_s>a\) with \(s>t\) exists, which is equivalent to \(L_a>t\). Counting \(t=1,\ldots,L_a-1\) gives the sum.
   622	Known gaps: Algebraic only. It does not replace the accepted truncation or Bayes-predictability criteria.
   623	Source: `iterations/iter_014/solver_attempt.md`.
