   692	## Lemma: Shared-type full-reveal saturation
   693	Status: plausible in the stated toy model
   694	Assumptions: Sequential blocks share one hidden type; block \(j\) has length \(D_j\), terminal reveal probability \(q_j\), and if a nonzero terminal event occurs then the hidden type is fully learned before later blocks. Zero terminal observations are noninformative.
   695	Statement candidate: The total unresolved Bayes-gap contribution is at most on the scale
   696	\[
   697	\sum_j D_jq_j\exp\left(-\sum_{k<j}q_k\right).
