   345	## Lemma: Density-form finite-prior support formula under domination
   346	Status: proved for finite priors in the completed prefix-kernel model
   347	Assumptions: Same fixed finite \(T,G\), public exogenous, and payoff-weighted reward-measure domination assumptions as the previous lemma; finite \(F\subset\Theta\) and prior \(\pi\in\Delta(F)\).
   348	Statement:
   349	\[
   350	\sup_{q\in Q}\sum_{\theta\in F}\pi_\theta L_\theta(q)
   351	=
   352	\sum_{t=1}^T\int \max_{a\in G}
   353	\sum_{\theta\in F}\pi_\theta f^\theta_{t,a}(h)\,d\lambda_t(h),
   354	\]
   355	where \(d\mu^\theta_{t,a}=f^\theta_{t,a}d\lambda_t\).
   356	Proof sketch: The objective is linear and separable over \(t\) and \(h\):
   357	\[
   358	\sum_\theta\pi_\theta L_\theta(q)
   359	=
   360	\sum_t\int\sum_{a\in G}q_{t,a}(h)
   361	\left(\sum_\theta\pi_\theta f^\theta_{t,a}(h)\right)d\lambda_t(h).
   362	\]
   363	For each \((t,h)\), maximizing over the simplex \(\Delta(G)\) chooses an arm attaining the finite maximum; finite \(G\) gives a measurable argmax. The reverse inequality holds by pointwise comparison.
   364	Known gaps: Iteration 12 identifies this density expression with the earlier conditional-probability Bayes envelope for finite \(F,G\); see the density-\(\Psi\) lemma below. This support formula still lives inside the completed prefix-kernel model and does not itself prove original-policy alignment.
