     8	\]
     9	Thus \(\beta(h)=\sup_{a<1}a^h=1\) for every \(h\).
    10	Why it matters: If the law is known, playing a maximizer of \(G_T(a)=\sum_{L=0}^{T-1}a(1-a^L)\) every round matches the fixed comparator in expectation, giving zero regret despite failed \(\beta\).
